-- title:
--   Rationality and closedness of a crossing point
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M\neq 0$ with $p\mid M$ but $p^{2}\nmid M$, let $H\le(\mathbb Z/M)^{\times}$ contain every unit whose image under `ZMod.unitsMap` for $(M/p)\mid M$ is $1$, with $M/p\neq 0$, and let $hj$ assert that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` lies in the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$. Let $\mathfrak X$ be a term of the Deligne–Rapoport package `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` for the two-chart integral model $X$ of level $\Gamma_H(M)$ over $R_p$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho\colon R_p\to A$ a ring map compatible with the structural map to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\rho_O\colon R_p\to O$, maximal ideal generated by $p$, together with $\mathrm{to}\kappa\colon O\to\kappa_A$ satisfying $\mathrm{to}\kappa\circ\rho_O=\mathrm{residue}\circ\rho$. Write $X_O$ for the base change of $X$ along $\rho_O$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two maps $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,0$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,1$, and $x_n=\mathfrak X.\mathrm{crossingPt}\,n\in X_O$ its image; assume $\xi_\infty\rightsquigarrow x_n$ and $\xi_0\rightsquigarrow x_n$, and assume there is a morphism $s\colon\operatorname{Spec}(O/\mathfrak m)\to X_O$ over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue map $O\to O/\mathfrak m$ carrying the closed point to $x_n$. Then the map $O\to\kappa(x_n)$ sending $o$ to the residue class of the germ at $x_n$ of the global section pulled back from $o$ along $X_O\to\operatorname{Spec}O$ is surjective, and $\{x_n\}$ is closed in $X_O$.
--
--   This is the rationality and closedness input for the crossing points of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model at level $\Gamma_H(M)$: a point of an $O$-scheme hit by a section of the closed fibre has residue field $O/\mathfrak m$ generated by the germs of elements of $O$, and is a closed point. It is used in the construction of oriented étale charts at such crossings, in [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart).
